00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:14,600
 What stage of behavior change is he or she in?"

37
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:22,040
 So go ahead and pause the video and then we'll go over this together.

38
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:27,520
 So the test maker was very thoughtful in this case and ordered the answer choices in the

39
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,320
 correct order for you.

40
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:33,840
 Now this doesn't always happen this way, but it's great when it does.

41
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:35,680
 So we'll take advantage of this.

42
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:41,160
 Pre-contemplation is when you're not even considering behavior change, contemplations

43
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:46,120
 when you're starting to consider it, preparation is when you're preparing to take steps to

44
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:54,600
 change, action is when you're engaged in physical action towards that behavior change, and maintenance

45
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,000
 is maintaining that changed behavior.

46
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,680
 And this is the classic, we looked at this cycle that happens when someone is going through

47
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:08,320
 some type of pivotal change in behavior in their lives.

48
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:13,280
 Now the behavior change in this example is to quit smoking.

49
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:17,880
 Now the patient says, "I don't have time for that," while they're actively opposed

50
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:18,880
 to it.

51
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:24,120
 And so they're not even considering quitting smoking at this time in their lives.

52
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:28,320
 So this would put them at the pre-contemplation stage.

53
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:33,240
 So the answer here is A. Now as a side note, when you're studying

